### create first customer
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Jane",
  "lastName": "Wanjiku",
  "nationalId": "12345678",
  "email": "jane@example.com",
  "phoneNumber": "0712345678",
  "openingBalance": 15000
}

### create second customer
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Brian",
  "lastName": "Otieno",
  "nationalId": "23456789",
  "email": "brian@example.com",
  "phoneNumber": "+254722000111",
  "openingBalance": 500
}

### transfer (replace the account numbers with the ones returned above)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fromAccount": "0149895421023",
  "toAccount": "0194624317827",
  "amount": 2500.50,
  "narration": "Rent"
}

### check balance
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/accounts/0149895421023/balance

### validation error
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": -3
}
